                            <enumeratedValues>
                                <enumeratedValue>
                                    <name>0</name>
                                    <description>The CFGTMR channel output is put to safe state when the CFGTMR counter is enabled and the CFGTMR channel output is enabled by Fault Control (CFGTMR_FMSEL[FCTRLMSEL]!=2&apos;b00 and CFGTMR_FCTRL[FEOSTS]=1&apos;b0) and PWM is enabled (CFGTMR_CSTS[PWMOENCHn] = 1&apos;b1). Otherwise the channel output is tristated.</description>
                                    <value>#0</value>
                                </enumeratedValue>
                                <enumeratedValue>
                                    <name>1</name>
                                    <description>The CFGTMR channel output state is retained when the channel is in output mode. The output channel is tristated when the channel is in input capture [DECMEN=1&apos;b0, CHCM=1&apos;b0, MSnB:MSnA=2&apos;b00] or dual edge capture mode [DECMEN=1&apos;b1].</description>
                                    <value>#1</value>
                                </enumeratedValue>
